 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nInconsistent SQL Generation for NOT Expressions in ClickHouse Dialect\n\nHey team,\n\nI've noticed an inconsistency in the SQL generation for NOT expressions when using the ClickHouse dialect. It seems like the handling of certain expressions isn't quite right, particularly when dealing with `GLOBAL IN` and `IS NULL/IS NOT NULL` cases.\n\nHere's a simple reproduction script to illustrate the issue:\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot import parse_one, exp\n\n# Example with GLOBAL IN\nexpr_global_in = parse_one(\"x GLOBAL IN (SELECT * FROM y)\")\nnot_expr_global_in = exp.Not(this=expr_global_in)\nprint(not_expr_global_in.sql(dialect='clickhouse'))  # Expected: \"x GLOBAL NOT IN (SELECT * FROM y)\"\n\n# Example with IS NULL\nexpr_is_null = parse_one(\"x IS NULL\")\nnot_expr_is_null = exp.Not(this=expr_is_null)\nprint(not_expr_is_null.sql(dialect='clickhouse'))  # Expected: \"x IS NOT NULL\"\n```\n\nThe expected output should correctly reflect the negation of the expressions, but it seems like the current implementation might not be handling these cases as expected. This could lead to incorrect SQL being generated, which is a bit concerning.\n\nWould appreciate any insights or suggestions on how we might address this!\n\nThanks!\n</issue>\n",
